<p>Title and rating share a row; stars are the accent; the description can hold a list; the button spans the card.</p>

<h2>Header</h2>
<p>A band with a heading, in the body of a post. Both generations of the card are covered — the older one with <code>kg-style-dark</code> / <code>-light</code> / <code>-accent</code> / <code>-image</code> and three sizes, and the current one (<code>kg-v2</code>), whose colours arrive inline from the editor and which can split into words and picture.</p>
{{#example code=false flush=true}}
<div class="im-content im-content-flush">
	<div class="kg-card kg-header-card kg-v2 kg-width-wide kg-layout-split" style="background-color: #0a0a0a" data-background-color="#0a0a0a"><div class="kg-header-card-content"><picture><img class="kg-header-card-image" src="{{demo.three.[1].feature_image}}" loading="lazy" alt=""></picture><div class="kg-header-card-text"><h2 class="kg-header-card-heading" style="color: #ffffff" data-text-color="#ffffff">Part two: leaving</h2><p class="kg-header-card-subheading" style="color: #ffffff" data-text-color="#ffffff">What four years of consulting taught me about saying no.</p><a href="#header" class="kg-header-card-button" style="background-color: #ffffff; color: #0a0a0a" data-button-color="#ffffff" data-button-text-color="#0a0a0a">Keep reading</a></div></div></div>
	<div class="kg-card kg-header-card kg-width-wide kg-size-small kg-style-accent"><h2 class="kg-header-card-header">An older header card, in the accent</h2><h3 class="kg-header-card-subheader">Small size. Still styled, because old posts still have them.</h3></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Signup</h2>
<p>The field and its button share one pill; focus thickens the pill's edge to ink. <code>loading</code>, <code>success</code> and <code>error</code> — the classes Ghost's members script puts on the form — swap the label for a spinner, the form for the thank-you, and show the error. Ghost removes this card for signed-in members on the server.</p>
{{#example code=false flush=true}}
<div class="im-content im-content-flush">
	<div class="kg-card kg-signup-card kg-width-wide" data-lexical-signup-form style="background-color: #f5f5f5; display: none"><div class="kg-signup-card-content"><div class="kg-signup-card-text kg-align-center"><h2 class="kg-signup-card-heading" style="color: #0a0a0a">One email when something lands.</h2><p class="kg-signup-card-subheading" style="color: #0a0a0a">Nothing else, ever. Unsubscribe in one click.</p><form class="kg-signup-card-form" data-members-form="signup" onsubmit="return false"><div class="kg-signup-card-fields"><input class="kg-signup-card-input" id="kg-email" data-members-email type="email" required placeholder="Your email" aria-label="Your email"><button class="kg-signup-card-button kg-style-accent" style="color: #ffffff" type="submit"><span class="kg-signup-card-button-default">Subscribe</span><span class="kg-signup-card-button-loading"></span></button></div><div class="kg-signup-card-success" style="color: #0a0a0a">Email sent! Check your inbox to complete your signup.</div><div class="kg-signup-card-error" style="color: #0a0a0a" data-members-error></div></form><p class="kg-signup-card-disclaimer" style="color: #0a0a0a">No spam. Unsubscribe anytime.</p></div></div></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Call to action</h2>
<p>The newest card. "Sponsored" is the system's mono caption on the card's top rule. <strong>Minimal</strong> puts a small picture beside the words; <strong>immersive</strong> stacks a large one above them with a full-width button. Eight grounds, from the same tints as the callout.</p>
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="im-content im-content-flush">
	<div class="kg-card kg-cta-card kg-cta-bg-grey kg-cta-minimal kg-cta-has-img" data-layout="minimal"><div class="kg-cta-sponsor-label-wrapper"><div class="kg-cta-sponsor-label"><span style="white-space: pre-wrap">Sponsored</span></div></div><div class="kg-cta-content"><div class="kg-cta-image-container"><a href="#call-to-action"><img src="{{demo.three.[2].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></a></div><div class="kg-cta-content-inner"><div class="kg-cta-text"><p><strong>Scratch orgs in one click.</strong> Spin up a clean Salesforce org from any branch, seeded with data, and throw it away when the pull request merges.</p></div><a href="#call-to-action" class="kg-cta-button kg-style-accent" style="color: #ffffff">Try it free</a></div></div></div>
	<div class="kg-card kg-cta-card kg-cta-bg-blue kg-cta-immersive kg-cta-centered kg-cta-has-img" data-layout="immersive"><div class="kg-cta-content"><div class="kg-cta-image-container"><img src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="kg-cta-content-inner"><div class="kg-cta-text"><p><strong>The Amalfi guide, as a PDF.</strong> Every stop on the road, with parking.</p></div><a href="#call-to-action" class="kg-cta-button">Get the guide</a></div></div></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Paywall</h2>
<p>Where a post is cut for non-members, Ghost prints its own upgrade box, styled inline in the site's accent. The system only rounds it and sets its font, so it sits with everything else; the wording and the button are Ghost's and follow your portal settings.</p>

<h2>Every card, one rhythm</h2>
<ul>
	<li>A card gets <strong>1.5 ×</strong> <code>--im-flow</code> above and below — a little more air than a paragraph.</li>
	<li>One radius (<code>--im-kg-radius</code>) and one padding (<code>--im-kg-pad</code>), set on <code>.kg-card</code>. Change them once.</li>
	<li>Boxes are a hairline, never a shadow; a card that is a link answers by filling, one surface deeper than it already is.</li>
	<li>Captions are centred, small, muted — and can hold links.</li>
</ul>
